course: dictionary
lesson: 10718
title: Unwanted
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Unwanted is an adjective made from un- and wanted. The prefix un- means not, so unwanted means not wanted. «The shop gave its unwanted toys to the charity.» The owner did not want the toys any more, so they were given away.
explain: The word can also mean not needed or not welcome. «She got unwanted attention from a stranger online.» Nobody asked for that attention, and it made her feel uneasy. If you get unwanted messages, tell an adult you trust.
explain: Check the meaning by looking at the words around it, then swap in your meaning. Put "not wanted" in the sentence instead: «Unwanted weeds grew across the path.» Weeds that nobody wants there still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
fact: Unwanted means not wanted, not needed or not welcome.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so unwanted is the word wanted with not in front of it.
fact: «Unwanted gifts» and «unwanted toys» can be given to charity or rescue centres.
fact: «Unwanted attention» is attention that someone did not want, and it is a reason to tell an adult.
fact: «Pest control» means killing unwanted animals such as rats or mice.
exercise: «The shop gave its unwanted toys to the charity.» What does unwanted mean here? | * Not wanted any more | Lost and found | Very expensive | Brand new
exercise: «She got unwanted messages online, so she told an adult.» What should you do if you get unwanted messages? | Keep them as a gift | Reply to every one | Read them out loud to your friends | * Tell an adult you trust
exercise: «Unwanted weeds grew across the garden path.» Find and copy the word that means not wanted. | across | path | garden | * unwanted
test: «Rescue centres can take back unwanted pets.» What does unwanted mean in «unwanted pets»? | Pets that are for sale | * Pets that nobody wants or needs any more | Pets that are sleeping | Pets that are very fast
test: Ravi says, "Unwanted means wanted with un in front, so it means very wanted." Is he right? | Yes, because un- means very | Yes, because it is a long word | * No, un- means not, so unwanted means not wanted | No, it means wanted twice
exam: Which phrase means attention that nobody asked for? | Happy surprise | Loud music | * Unwanted attention | Wanted gift
